# Zero-legacy manifest for aien-dev/aien-train (#43).
# Read by aien-architecture-mv tools/zero-legacy/closure.om: `closure . release .zero-legacy`.
# Only lines starting with a kind word (data, generated, external, skip) are read;
# prefixes are relative to the repository root, first match wins.
# Every entry below is a recorded run artifact (exit codes, stdout/stderr, traces,
# hashes, sealed fixtures, vocabularies) that no program executes.
# Directories are declared whole only when they hold no .om, script or other source file,
# so no source file is declared as data. Wolfram oracle scripts (.wl) are not declared:
# they are verification oracles and need a reviewed exception, not a data claim.
